    {
      "id": "Localizable::My Hermes WebUI is refusing chats with \"Hermes Agent was updated while Hermes WebUI was running.\" Please do only this:\n1. Check that no Hermes update is still running and the last one finished without errors. If it didn't, stop and tell me.\n2. Restart the Hermes WebUI server the same way it was started (systemd, launchd, ctl.sh, Docker, or whatever runs it). Don't update, reinstall, or reconfigure anything.\n3. Confirm it's back: its `/health` endpoint should return 200.\n\nIf it doesn't come back up, show me the last lines of its error log and suggest a fix, but don't change config, environment variables, or Hermes source until I say so.",
      "catalog": "Localizable",
      "key": "My Hermes WebUI is refusing chats with \"Hermes Agent was updated while Hermes WebUI was running.\" Please do only this:\n1. Check that no Hermes update is still running and the last one finished without errors. If it didn't, stop and tell me.\n2. Restart the Hermes WebUI server the same way it was started (systemd, launchd, ctl.sh, Docker, or whatever runs it). Don't update, reinstall, or reconfigure anything.\n3. Confirm it's back: its `/health` endpoint should return 200.\n\nIf it doesn't come back up, show me the last lines of its error log and suggest a fix, but don't change config, environment variables, or Hermes source until I say so.",
      "units": [
        {
          "source": "My Hermes WebUI is refusing chats with \"Hermes Agent was updated while Hermes WebUI was running.\" Please do only this:\n1. Check that no Hermes update is still running and the last one finished without errors. If it didn't, stop and tell me.\n2. Restart the Hermes WebUI server the same way it was started (systemd, launchd, ctl.sh, Docker, or whatever runs it). Don't update, reinstall, or reconfigure anything.\n3. Confirm it's back: its `/health` endpoint should return 200.\n\nIf it doesn't come back up, show me the last lines of its error log and suggest a fix, but don't change config, environment variables, or Hermes source until I say so."
        }
      ],
      "sourceStructure": null,
      "placeholders": [],
      "protectedTerms": [
        "Hermes",
        "WebUI"
      ],
      "comment": null,
      "extractionState": null,
      "surface": "shared-catalog",
      "sourceReferences": [],
      "target": null
